\cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Three laser-editing pain points reported during authoring: (a) once a slam is attached to a laser, the Smooth/Linear/Step interpolation menu appears to do nothing on the connecting line, because interp is stored as the OUTGOING type from a point and a slam segment always renders as a slam regardless of interp; (b) two laser segments that visually touch at the same tick/position remain separate sections with a visible break instead of forming one continuous laser; (c) lasers and isolated slams give no visual cue of where they start, where they end, or which direction a slam flicks, unlike the SDVX in-game / KSM Editor presentation. The fix should make the interp menu operate on the visible (non-slam) segment adjacent to the clicked anchor, auto-merge touching sections regardless of junction type, and draw SDVX-style entry tails, exit heads, and slam direction arrows in the 2D editor.\
Status: SHIPPED in v0.0.32. (a) resolveLaserInterpTarget() retargets the interp menu/Alt+click to the adjacent non-slam segment; stale menu handler leak fixed. (b) ChartData.autoConnectLasers() merges touching sections (slam/smooth/normal), wired via autoConnectLasersFixup() with active-draw ref preservation. (c) Renderer._drawLaserSectionCaps() draws entry tail, exit head, and white slam direction arrows. Logic unit-tested.\
