Point 14 (New Recommended: Freehand Laser Drawing)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The system specification states that "Holding Shift allows freeform drawing that is later simplified into smooth curves." This mode was partially scaffolded (_rdpSimplify function and drag.freehand flag defined) but never wired up. The feature should allow a chartist to hold Shift while pressing the laser tool and drag across the lane to sketch a freehand path. A live semi-transparent polyline preview should follow the cursor during the drag. On mouse-up, the raw collected points are run through Ramer-Douglas-Peucker simplification to remove noise while preserving intentional curves. The simplified set of anchor points is committed as a new laser section. Freehand drawing should always start a fresh section (not extend an existing one), and should respect Laser Mirror Mode by simultaneously creating a mirrored path on the opposite side. This completes the spec-required "freeform drawing" path for the laser tool.\
Status: SHIPPED in v0.0.35; quality overhaul in v0.0.36. v0.0.35 wired the basic gesture. v0.0.36 fixed the curve quality: raw unsnapped capture (_freehandSample), moving-average de-jitter (_smoothFreehandV), scale-correct vertical-deviation RDP (_rdpSimplifyV), Catmull-Rom resampling (_catmullV) that densifies only curved spans, automatic slam detection, and a blue crosshair cursor (FREEHAND_CURSOR + _updateFreehandCursor) when a laser tool is active with Shift held. Mirror Mode mirrors the smoothed spline. Math unit-tested (10 assertions pass). APP_VERSION = 0.0.36.\
